meta {
  name: Create embedding
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/v1/embeddings
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "{{model}}",
    "input": "Say PONG"
  }
}

docs {
  Synchronous, not queued — no OpenAI client expects to poll for an
  embedding. Unlike **List models** this still costs the upstream real
  compute, so it goes through `throttle:queue` (`BACKLOG_RATE_LIMIT`) the
  same as **Queue chat completion**.

  Anthropic has no embeddings API; a gateway pointed at one answers with
  Anthropic's own `404`, passed through under `error.type: upstream_error`.
}
